## Summary
After renaming a session alias (codex-black-sledge-* -> gk-black) and re-registering on the public relay, `c2c monitor` relay watch fails open→terminal with a fixed ~30.5s timestamp skew even though the host clock is NTP-synced and matches relay HTTP Date to the second. Local inbox watch continues; same-host DMs work.

## Environment
- host: linux (Australia/Sydney)
- c2c client 0.12.0 (git_hash fd5eac2 observed via relay status)
- relay: https://relay.c2c.im
- alias: gk-black (session CLI)
- node_id/session_id after register: cli-gk-black
- timedatectl: System clock synchronized: yes; NTP active
- curl -sI https://relay.c2c.im Date header matched local UTC second-for-second at failure window

## Sequence observed (2026-07-13 ~11:32 UTC)
1. `c2c rename` to gk-black succeeded (local).
2. `c2c monitor` started; identity line: monitoring as gk-black; relay watch peek cli-gk-black/cli-gk-black every 5.0s
3. First failure after rename (before re-register): unauthorized: alias "gk-black" has no identity binding → TERMINAL, relay watch disabled
4. `c2c relay register --alias=gk-black` → ok, lease alive
5. Restart monitor → peek starts
6. Transient: nonce_replay: request nonce replay (attempt 1, then 2; backing off)
7. TERMINAL: timestamp_out_of_window: request ts skew -30.5s outside window
8. Same TERMINAL pattern on a second monitor restart (~21:33 AEST / 11:33 UTC) after another register: skew again exactly -30.5s after nonce_replay backoff

## Parallel whoami / register notes
- `c2c whoami --relay` after register: often "registered_unreachable — relay lease alive but no live connector bridge — inbound relay traffic will not reach this broker"
- connector reported down, last sync ~1.4d (a long-lived `c2c relay connect` process was present on the host)
- At one intermediate moment whoami also reported: Ed25519 request signature does not verify
- Register itself returns ok with receipt

## Expected
- After alias rename + register, relay peek for cli-<alias> should succeed or degrade with actionable recoverable errors
- Clock-skew errors should not fire when host NTP and relay HTTP Date agree
- nonce_replay during peek backoff should not poison subsequent signed request timestamps into a permanent -30.5s skew TERMINAL that requires manual re-register + monitor restart

## Actual
- Relay watch enters TERMINAL timestamp_out_of_window (-30.5s) and self-disables
- Local inbox continues (good)
- Cross-host receive via monitor is dead until operator intervenes; re-register does not reliably prevent the next cycle

## Impact
Agents that depend on relay for cross-host DMs lose inbound relay after rename/register; false "fix the clock" guidance when clock is fine; noisy ops during multi-agent handoffs.

## Repro sketch
1. On a machine with live local broker + configured public relay
2. Rename session alias to a new unused alias
3. Start `c2c monitor` (relay watch peeks cli-<alias>/<alias>)
4. Observe identity-binding failure if not yet registered
5. `c2c relay register --alias=<new>`
6. Restart monitor
7. Watch for nonce_replay then timestamp_out_of_window -30.5s TERMINAL

## Notes for fix investigation
- Skew magnitude is suspiciously constant at -30.5s across restarts
- Failure only after nonce_replay backoff path — possible stale signed request / reused ts under backoff
- Connector bridge liveness vs CLI register/peek identity may be split incorrectly after rename